# Memory index

Only the gotchas you would get wrong without them. Installation diaries and project status
do not belong here - they age into noise and push the useful lines off the first screen.

**This file is authored, not mirrored.** It is written by hand and grouped the way you
actually think about your tools. A sync script may warn that a file on disk has no line
here; it must never write the line for you. The judgement is the whole value. The hook
after each link is the file's `description`, verbatim - one relevance text per memory -
and `Assert-MemoryIndex.ps1` fails when the two differ.

**Method and verification discipline do not live here.** They go to
`<LESSONS-PATH>/LESSONS.md`. This file is tools and projects only.

